      "title": "ci: skip tests:coverage when a test job fails",
      "body": "## What\n\n`tests:coverage` now uses its own rules (default `on_success`) instead of inheriting `.test`'s `when: always`.\n\n## Why\n\nIn pipeline https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/pipelines/3039029416, `tests:unit` failed with `runner_system_failure`, yet `tests:coverage` still ran and failed on the missing `coverage-unit.txt`. With `on_success`, coverage is skipped while a test job is failed and runs automatically once the retry passes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
