      "kind": "pull_request",
      "title": "fix: avoid unsupported telemetry properties on older GitLab instances",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses gitlab-org/cli#8710.\n\nCheck the target GitLab instance version through the metadata API before sending the `additional_properties` field with `usage_data/track_event`.\n\n- GitLab 19.4 and newer continue to receive the existing CLI attribution properties.\n- Older versions receive the base telemetry event without `additional_properties`, avoiding repeated `InvalidPropertyError` entries in their instance logs.\n- If the metadata request fails or the version cannot be parsed, omit the optional properties conservatively while still attempting to send the base event.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Cover versions before and at the 19.4 compatibility boundary, newer major versions, and unknown/malformed versions.\n- Cover telemetry sent to an 18.11 instance, asserting that `additional_properties` is omitted.\n- Existing telemetry tests use a metadata response for a current 19.6 instance.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe code and tests are committed to the source branch. CI is requested to run the repository's checks; no local test run is claimed.",
      "state": "open",
      "stateRaw": "opened",
      "isDraft": false,
